<item>
            <title>[LUDOC-576] Document per-net srpc.flavor rules with LNet Dynamic Peer Discovery</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LUDOC-576</link>
                <project id="10070" key="LUDOC">Lustre Documentation</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Two manual sections describe per-net flavor rules, &lt;tt&gt;&amp;lt;target&amp;gt;.srpc.flavor.&amp;lt;network&amp;gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;.&amp;lt;direction&amp;gt;&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;=&amp;lt;flavor&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;. The sections are &quot;Managing Security in a Lustre File System&quot; and &quot;Lustre Shared Secret Key&quot;. Add a note about Multi-Rail and LNet Dynamic Peer Discovery to both sections.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The note must say these items:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A per-net rule matches the net of the primary NID of the other side. The rule does not match the net that an RPC uses.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The client uses the primary NID of the server. The server uses the primary NID of the client.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;With discovery on, a primary NID can be on any net of the node, and it can change.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Give the same flavor to each net that a client and a server share. Otherwise the two sides can select different flavors. The server then refuses the RPCs with &quot;unauthorized rpc flavor&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The &apos;network&apos; mount option restricts the nets that a client sends on. With discovery on, the primary NID of the client can still be on another net. To select a flavor for the net of a tenant, keep discovery off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Related tickets: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20403&quot; title=&quot;Refresh import conn on primary migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20403&quot;&gt;LU-20403&lt;/a&gt; (removes the lock of the primary NID), &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20384&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: sptlrpc per-network flavor rules never match (only default applies)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20384&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20384&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (per-net rules match again), and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20921&quot; title=&quot;sptlrpc: per-net flavor rules do not follow the net of the RPCs with Multi-Rail&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20921&quot;&gt;LU-20921&lt;/a&gt; (future work).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
